== d1. Stripe82 (z < 0.2): dynamical-mass inequality  q = log Mdyn - log(M* + M_CO,gas + M_HI)
  N 78; q median -0.10 16th pct -0.30 min -0.71; share with q < 0: 0.679; share violating at 2 sigma (q + 2 sigma_Mdyn < 0): 0.167 (Mdyn errors 0.14-0.26 dex)
  common upward shift of the CO gas mass at which 16% of the galaxies violate q < 0: -1.0 dex (the allowed one-sided common-mode scale)
  without HI: share with q<0 0.474
  share violating q < 0 versus a common shift of the CO gas mass (dex): {-1.0: 0.5897435897435898, -0.5: 0.6025641025641025, 0.0: 0.6794871794871795, 0.3: 0.7564102564102564, 0.6: 0.8461538461538461}; note: Stripe82's M_dyn is the mass enclosed in the CO-emitting region while M* and the integrated HI are galaxy totals (aperture mismatch), so the inequality is not a clean bound
  [PASS] H-C17b Stripe82 share with M* + M_CO + M_HI > M_dyn: 0.679 (estimate: at least 0.10)

== d1b. Stripe82 gas phase (D15): d = logM_CO - logM_gas,dust (H2+He vs total gas); d' adds the HI to the CO side
  d: N 78 mean -0.068 SD 0.155; d' (CO + HI vs dust gas): N 78 mean +0.421 SD 0.199 SE 0.023; K(d') 0.212
  HI share of (CO + HI) gas: median 0.63; HI > CO in 0.77 of the galaxies
  [PASS] H-C25 d' mean +0.421 (opposite sign to d = -0.068, |d'| > 0.10)

